What each column means
Column	Meaning	Example	Need it?
STATEFP	State code. Virginia is always 51	51	No, it’s the same in every row
COUNTYFP	County or independent city code (133 of them in Virginia)	025	Yes, for labeling and regional grouping
TRACTCE	The tract’s own 6-digit number within its county	930302	No, it’s already inside GEOID
GEOID	The tract’s unique ID: state + county + tract	51025930302	Yes, the most important column
GEOIDFQ	The same ID with a prefix, 1400000US	1400000US51025930302	Yes, and useful (see below)
NAME	Short tract number	9303.02	No
NAMELSAD	Readable name	Census Tract 9303.02	Yes, for labels
MTFCC	Census feature type code	G5020	No, it’s the same in every row (means “census tract”)
FUNCSTAT	Functional status	S	No, it’s the same in every row
ALAND	Land area in square meters	342689262	Yes, to remove water-only tracts
AWATER	Water area in square meters	2060807	Optional
INTPTLAT, INTPTLON	Latitude and longitude of the tract’s internal point	+36.64, -077.95	Optional (only if you use a point-based method)
